# A request sock resends its SYN-ACK when the handshake's ACK does not
# come: after 1 s, then 2 s more (RFC 6298 5.5), the same options each
# time; the late ACK still completes the connection.
# Copyright (C) 2026 The LikeOS Project
0.000 socket s stream
0.000 bind s 8080
0.000 listen s 16
0.100 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
0.100 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
1.100 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
3.100 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
3.200 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 3200 ecr echo>
3.200 accept s c
3.210 state c ESTABLISHED
